[Event "✨Pirc/Czech System for Black: Lifetime Repertoire⁉️✨ 👀 🦾💖: London Bridge is Falling Down!"]
[Date "2021.02.23"]
[Result "*"]
[Variant "Standard"]
[ECO "A40"]
[Opening "Queen's Pawn Game"]
[StudyName "✨Pirc/Czech System for Black: Lifetime Repertoire⁉️✨ 👀 🦾💖"]
[ChapterName "London Bridge is Falling Down!"]
[ChapterURL "https://lichess.org/study/nRiq9SZx/UC9lPnjY"]
[Annotator "https://lichess.org/@/WatsonChenney"]
[UTCDate "2021.02.23"]
[UTCTime "20:39:38"]

1. d4 { 🚫 Oh no! White played the best move, and they intend to absolutely crush us with the London 🇬🇧 Will we survive?? 😱 } 1... c6 { Not to worry, we got it covered! } 2. Bf4 { Here is you are already familiar with "anti-London" variations, you probably want to play Nf6 or even Qb6 → try that out - next time! For now we'll stick with the plan. [Note: technically you could play d6 and then c6, but I prefer c6 first.] } 2... d6 3. e3?! { Umm, I don't know whaat to do! Ok, better just continue with our normal London. It's in the book 📚 🤷🏼 } { [%csl Re3] } (3. Nf3 Nf6 { With the standard ideas against the London. } { [%csl Bf8,Gg7,Bd8,Gb6][%cal Bf8g7,Bg7g6,Gd8b6] } (3... h6 { Another super sharp idea. } { [%csl Rg7,Rg5][%cal Rg7g5] })) 3... g5!? { Baam! Ok, you can also just play Nf6 or Qb6, but this is a nasty surprise weapon, or sideline to use against <9000 players. } { [%csl Gf4,Gg3][%cal Gf4g3] } (3... Nf6 { A solid idea as well, especially if your idea is to go after the bishop. } { [%csl Gf6,Rh5,Rf4,Rg3][%cal Rf6h5,Bh5f4] }) (3... Qb6 { [%csl Rb2,Gb6][%cal Bb6b2] }) 4. Bg3 $7 (4. Bxg5?? Qa5+ { Winning the bishop, and trust me, people still fall for this! } { [%csl Ba5,Rg5][%cal Ra5e1,Ra5g5] }) 4... h5!? { The logical continuation, gaining space on the Kingside, and threatening to trap the bishop. } 5. h4 (5. Nf3?? h4 { [%csl Rh4,Rg3][%cal Rh4g3] }) (5. h3 { Both moves are fine for White. } 5... h4) 5... g4 { And the arrows illustrate a sample development strategy for Black. This is just one line to choose for Black, move 3..Nf6 and 3...Qb6 are certainly more solid for normal play. If White plays 3.Nf3, be sure to check the above sidelines for that on how to play. } { [%csl Gg8,Gf8,Gd8,Rb6,Rg7,Rh6,Gc8,Rf5,Gb8,Rd7][%cal Bg8h6,Bf8g7,Bd8b6,Bc8f5,Bb8d7] } *


[Event "✨Pirc/Czech System for Black: Lifetime Repertoire⁉️✨ 👀 🦾💖: Czech: The Old Indian"]
