1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 d6 { Trying to reach our position via the Philidor position main move order is a bit sus 🤨 } 3. d4 (3. Bc4 Be7 4. d4 exd4 5. Nxd4 Nf6 6. Nc3 { Fine, but not what we wanted. }) 3... Nf6!? 4. Nc3 (4. dxe5! Nxe4 5. Qd5 Nc5 6. Bg5 { And I already don't like our position so much. }) 4... Nbd7 5. Bc4 (5. dxe5 dxe5 6. Bc4 $10) 5... Be7 6. O-O c6 7. a4 Qc7 8. Re1 (8. h3 h6 9. Be3) 8... h6 9. h3 Nf8 10. Be3 g5 { We were lucky to make it this far! 😅 In the next chapter we'll look at further reasons why the Philidor move order is not to be preferred. } *


